---
description: TypeScript implementation rules and best practices
globs: *.tsx,*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---
# TypeScript Implementation Rules

<rule>
name: atlas_typescript
description: Standards for implementing proper TypeScript patterns and best practices
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:ts|tsx)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)typescript|interface|type|enum|generics"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing TypeScript code:

      ## Type Safety
      - Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
      - Use strict type checking options
      - Avoid using `any` type
      - Use proper type assertions
      - Implement proper type guards

      ## Type Definitions
      - Prefer `interface` over `type` when possible
      - Define proper type aliases
      - Use proper generics
      - Implement proper utility types
      - Use proper mapped types

      ## Type-Safe Development
      - Use proper type inference
      - Implement proper type narrowing
      - Use proper discriminated unions
      - Implement proper type predicates
      - Use proper conditional types

      ## API Types
      - Define proper request/response types
      - Use proper enum types
      - Implement proper type utilities
      - Use proper type composition
      - Implement proper type validation

      ## Node.js Development
      - Target Node.js v20+ features
      - Use ES modules
      - Implement proper error handling
      - Follow Node.js best practices
      - Use async/await for asynchronous operations

      ## Code Organization
      - Use proper module boundaries
      - Implement clear interfaces
      - Follow SOLID principles
      - Use dependency injection
      - Maintain consistent file structure

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new TypeScript component"
    output: "Component uses proper interfaces, type guards, and follows TypeScript best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>